const TB_SHORT=[P(`硬骨魚`,`Bony fish`),P(`軟骨魚`,`Cartilage fish`),P(`兩生`,`Amphibian`),P(`爬蟲`,`Reptile`),P(`鳥`,`Bird`),P(`哺乳`,`Mammal`),P(`刺絲胞`,`Cnidarian`),P(`扁形`,`Flatworm`),P(`軟體`,`Mollusc`),P(`環節`,`Annelid`),P(`節肢`,`Arthropod`),P(`棘皮`,`Echinoderm`)];
const TB_NAMES=[
 P(`硬骨魚類：用鰓呼吸，卵產在水裡，體溫跟著水溫變`,`Bony fish: gills, eggs laid in water, body temperature follows the water`),
 P(`軟骨魚類：骨骼是軟骨，體內受精，生法因種而異`,`Cartilage fish: a skeleton of cartilage, internal fertilization, and several ways of having young`),
 P(`兩生類：幼體用鰓，成體用肺，卵產在水裡`,`Amphibians: gills when young, lungs as adults, eggs laid in water`),
 P(`爬蟲類：用肺呼吸，體內受精，產有殼的卵`,`Reptiles: lungs, internal fertilization, shelled eggs`),
 P(`鳥類：肺加氣囊，硬殼卵，是恆溫動物`,`Birds: lungs plus air sacs, hard-shelled eggs, endotherms`),
 P(`哺乳類：用肺呼吸，多數胎生，是恆溫動物`,`Mammals: lungs, mostly live birth, endotherms`),
 P(`刺絲胞動物：身體很薄，直接從體表交換氣體`,`Cnidarians: a thin body that exchanges gases through its surface`),
 P(`扁形動物：身體扁平很薄，從體表交換氣體`,`Flatworms: a flat, thin body that exchanges gases through its surface`),
 P(`軟體動物：水生的用鰓，陸生的蝸牛用肺`,`Molluscs: gills in water, a lung in the land snail`),
 P(`環節動物：蚯蚓靠潮濕的體表交換氣體`,`Annelids: an earthworm exchanges gases through its moist skin`),
 P(`節肢動物：氣管、書肺或鰓，因種類而不同`,`Arthropods: tracheae, book lungs or gills, depending on the kind`),
 P(`棘皮動物：皮鰓和管足，精卵排到海水裡受精`,`Echinoderms: skin gills and tube feet, sperm and eggs meet in the sea`)];
const TB_TEXT=[
 P(`硬骨魚類用鰓呼吸。多數魚的卵和精子都排到水裡，在體外受精，卵在水中發育，所以是卵生。體溫會隨環境改變，是變溫動物。（少數魚如孔雀魚是體內受精。）例子：鯉魚、鮭魚。`,`Bony fish breathe with gills. In most, eggs and sperm are released into the water and meet outside the body, and the eggs develop in the water, so they lay eggs. Body temperature changes with the surroundings, so they are ectotherms. (A few fish, such as guppies, fertilize internally.) Examples: carp, salmon.`),
 P(`軟骨魚類的骨骼是軟骨，用鰓呼吸，鰓裂直接露在身體兩側。牠們是體內受精：有的下蛋（卵生），有的卵在母體內孵化，有的直接生下小魚（胎生），因種類而不同。體溫是變溫。例子：鯊魚、魟、鰩。`,`Cartilage fish have a skeleton of cartilage and breathe with gills whose slits open on the sides of the body. Fertilization is internal: some lay eggs, some hatch the eggs inside the mother, and some give birth to live young, depending on the kind. They are ectotherms. Examples: sharks, stingrays.`),
 P(`兩生類的幼體（蝌蚪）生活在水中，用鰓呼吸；成體用肺，潮濕的皮膚也能幫忙交換氣體。多數是體外受精，卵沒有硬殼，要產在水裡，孵出的幼體要經過變態才變成成體。體溫是變溫。（少數如蠑螈是體內受精。）例子：青蛙、蟾蜍。`,`The young of amphibians (tadpoles) live in water and breathe with gills; adults use lungs, and moist skin helps with gas exchange. Most fertilize externally; the eggs have no hard shell and must be laid in water, and the young go through metamorphosis to become adults. They are ectotherms. (A few, such as salamanders, fertilize internally.) Examples: frogs, toads.`),
 P(`爬蟲類用肺呼吸，體表有鱗片，皮膚乾燥。牠們是體內受精，卵有殼，可以產在陸地上，孵出來的幼體像小成體，不需要變態。體溫是變溫。（少數蛇和蜥蜴的卵在母體內孵化。）例子：斑龜、蜥蜴、蛇。`,`Reptiles breathe with lungs and have scales and dry skin. Fertilization is internal, and the eggs are shelled and can be laid on land; the young look like small adults and do not go through metamorphosis. They are ectotherms. (In a few snakes and lizards the eggs hatch inside the mother.) Examples: turtles, lizards, snakes.`),
 P(`鳥類有肺，還有氣囊：氣囊協助通氣，氣體交換仍在肺裡。牠們是體內受精，產硬殼的卵，由親鳥孵卵。體溫大致穩定，不太受環境溫度影響，是恆溫動物。特色：羽毛、前肢變成翅膀、骨頭中空、有瞬膜。例子：小白鷺、企鵝。`,`Birds have lungs and air sacs: the air sacs help ventilation, while gas exchange is still in the lungs. Fertilization is internal, the eggs have hard shells, and the parents incubate them. Body temperature stays fairly steady whatever the surroundings, so birds are endotherms. Features: feathers, forelimbs turned into wings, hollow bones, a nictitating membrane. Examples: little egret, penguin.`),
 P(`哺乳類用肺呼吸，體內受精，多數是胎生，母體用乳汁哺育幼體。（鴨嘴獸和針鼴是卵生，仍是哺乳類。）體溫穩定，是恆溫動物。特色：毛髮、乳汁。例子：亞洲象、蝙蝠、虎鯨。`,`Mammals breathe with lungs, fertilize internally and mostly give birth to live young, which the mother feeds with milk. (The platypus and echidnas lay eggs and are still mammals.) Body temperature is steady, so they are endotherms. Features: hair and milk. Examples: Asian elephant, bat, killer whale.`),
 P(`水母、海葵、珊瑚沒有特別的呼吸器官，身體壁很薄，氧氣直接從體表進出。受精方式因種類而不同；卵發育成幼蟲，再長成成體。體溫是變溫。特色：刺絲胞、一個開口、輻射對稱。例子：水母、海葵、珊瑚。`,`Jellyfish, sea anemones and corals have no special breathing organ; the body wall is thin, so oxygen passes straight through the surface. How fertilization happens differs from kind to kind; the egg grows into a larva, then into an adult. They are ectotherms. Features: cnidocytes, one opening, radial symmetry. Examples: jellyfish, sea anemone, coral.`),
 P(`渦蟲身體扁平又薄，氧氣直接從體表進出。牠們雌雄同體，交配後在體內受精，產卵。體溫是變溫。特色：腹背扁平、再生能力強。例子：渦蟲、絛蟲。`,`A planarian has a flat, thin body, and oxygen passes straight through its surface. It has both sexes in one body, fertilizes internally after mating, and lays eggs. It is an ectotherm. Features: a flattened body, strong powers of regeneration. Examples: planarian, tapeworm.`),
 P(`水生的軟體動物（章魚、貝類）用鰓呼吸，陸生的蝸牛用肺。受精方式因種類而不同：章魚是體內受精，許多貝類把精卵排到水中受精。大多是卵生。體溫是變溫。特色：身體柔軟、不分節、有肌肉足，有些有殼。例子：章魚、蝸牛、文蛤。`,`Water molluscs (octopus, clams) breathe with gills; the land snail uses a lung. Fertilization differs: an octopus fertilizes internally, while many clams release sperm and eggs into the water. Most lay eggs. They are ectotherms. Features: a soft unsegmented body and a muscular foot; some have a shell. Examples: octopus, snail, clam.`),
 P(`蚯蚓沒有鰓也沒有肺，靠潮濕的體表交換氣體，所以皮膚乾掉就會悶死。牠們雌雄同體，兩條蚯蚓交配、互換精子，之後卵在環帶分泌的卵繭裡受精、發育。體溫是變溫。特色：身體由許多環節重複排成。例子：蚯蚓、沙蠶、水蛭。`,`An earthworm has neither gills nor lungs; it exchanges gases through its moist skin, so it suffocates if the skin dries out. It has both sexes in one body: two worms mate and swap sperm, and then the eggs are fertilized and develop in a cocoon made by the clitellum. It is an ectotherm. Feature: a body built of many repeated rings. Examples: earthworm, sandworm, leech.`),
 P(`節肢動物的呼吸構造因種類而不同：昆蟲用氣管，蜘蛛用書肺，蝦、蟹用鰓。多數是體內受精，卵生。體溫是變溫。特色：外骨骼、附肢分節，長大要蛻殼。例子：蜻蜓、蜘蛛、蟹。`,`The breathing organ of arthropods depends on the kind: insects use tracheae, spiders use book lungs, shrimps and crabs use gills. Most fertilize internally and lay eggs. They are ectotherms. Features: an exoskeleton, jointed limbs, and molting to grow. Examples: dragonfly, spider, crab.`),
 P(`海星在背面的皮膚上有小突起（皮鰓），再加上管足，用來交換氣體。多數是體外受精：精子和卵排到海水裡相遇。卵發育成浮游的幼蟲，再變成成體。體溫是變溫。特色：棘、管足、成體五輻對稱。例子：海星、海膽、海參。`,`A sea star has small skin projections on its upper side (skin gills), together with tube feet, for gas exchange. Most fertilize externally: sperm and eggs meet in the sea water. The egg grows into a drifting larva, then into the adult. It is an ectotherm. Features: spines, tube feet, five-fold radial symmetry as an adult. Examples: sea star, sea urchin, sea cucumber.`)];

